  "goodToKnow": "Die Altersvorsorge is retirement provision. Germany's system rests on three pillars: the statutory pension (gesetzliche Rente), occupational pensions (betriebliche Altersvorsorge) and private saving, such as the state-subsidised Riester-Rente (2002). With an ageing population, experts warn of a Rentenlücke (pension gap), and ETFs have become popular. Die Vorsorge means precaution, also medical check-ups. It has no plural."
